ALLOCATE MINIMUM NUMBER OF PAGES
📌 Problem Statement

You are given an array pages[] where each element represents pages in a book.

You must allocate books to M students such that:

Each student gets at least one book

Books are allocated contiguously

The maximum pages assigned to a student is minimized

Return that minimum possible maximum.

📌 Example
pages = [12, 34, 67, 90]
M = 2

Output: 113


👉 Allocation:

Student 1 → [12, 34, 67] → 113

Student 2 → [90]

💡 Key Insight

This is not DP, it is:

🔥 Binary Search on Answer

🧠 Search Space

Minimum = max(pages[])

Maximum = sum(pages[])

We binary search this range.

⚙️ Algorithm

Set:

low = max(pages)
high = sum(pages)


While low ≤ high:

mid = possible max pages

Check if allocation is possible with mid

If possible → try smaller value

Else → increase value

🔍 Feasibility Check (Greedy)

Assign books sequentially

If pages exceed mid, assign to next student

Count students needed

🧩 Java Code (Placement-Ready)
class Solution {

    public int findPages(int[] pages, int m) {
        if (m > pages.length) return -1;

        int low = 0, high = 0;
        for (int p : pages) {
            low = Math.max(low, p);
            high += p;
        }

        int ans = -1;
        while (low <= high) {
            int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;

            if (isPossible(pages, m, mid)) {
                ans = mid;
                high = mid - 1;
            } else {
                low = mid + 1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }

    private boolean isPossible(int[] pages, int students, int maxPages) {
        int count = 1, sum = 0;

        for (int p : pages) {
            sum += p;
            if (sum > maxPages) {
                count++;
                sum = p;
                if (count > students) return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}

